+
+## Memberships and joined callbacks
+
+Bots start with no open-room memberships. The new/edit form's **Add to all open rooms**
+checkbox is off by default. Enabling it grants all existing open rooms and opts into future
+open rooms (including rooms changed from closed to open). Disabling it removes only the opt-in,
+not existing memberships. Open-room new/edit forms provide bot checkboxes for selective access,
+while opted-in bots remain selected and disabled. Only bot memberships are changed by this
+picker; omitted picker parameters preserve memberships for older clients. Closed rooms keep
+the existing user picker. People still automatically join open rooms. Existing installations
+keep their existing bot memberships, with automatic joining off until explicitly enabled.
+
+`Room::grant_to` records a bot's first non-direct membership in `chat_bot_room_joins` and emits
+`Event::BotJoined` after commit. Both manual and automatic grants use this path. Unique
+bot/room keys prevent duplicate greetings on repeated saves, duplicate grants, or removal and
+re-addition. Direct conversations do not record or emit joins. No historical notifications
+are sent on upgrade, and configuring a webhook does not replay past joins.
+
+```json
+{
+  "event": "joined",
+  "room": { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/42-Xy3abc9defGh/messages" }
+}
+```
+
+The joined job shares the mention HTTP delivery and reply pipeline, including timeouts,
+sanitization, permission rechecks, and bot-authored message broadcasts. There is no request
+host in this database-triggered job, so broadcasts render relative URLs. Deduplication is
+persistent, but network delivery retains the existing best-effort job semantics: no retries,
+and no guarantee of delivery after crashes, queue overflow, or endpoint failures. A bot
+without a webhook at delivery time receives no callback.
+
+Regression commands:
+
+- `cargo test -p campfire_db`
+- `cargo test -p campfire bots`
